ManagerResponse class provides information about a leave request, such as its status, and whether it has been approved or rejected.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nmore\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nThe Leave API also includes a couple of API endpoints:\\n \\n\\n GET /leave\\n \\n\\n Creates a new leave request, or updates an existing leave request, or views the details of a leave request.\\n \\n\\n PUT /leave/{id}\\n \\n\\n Creates a new leave request, or updates an existing leave request, or views the details of a leave request.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\ncontinue\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nThe Leave API also includes a couple of controller classes:\\n \\n\\n LeaveController\\n LeaveRequestController\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nmore\", \"response\": \"The LeaveController class provides methods for creating, updating, deleting and viewing leave requests, and for checking whether a leave request has been approved or rejected. The LeaveRequestController class provides methods for creating, updating, deleting and viewing leave requests, and for checking whether a leave request has been approved or rejected.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/633", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"What is the chemical symbol for Si?\", \"response\": \"The chemical symbol for silicon is Si. Silicon is a chemical element with the atomic number 14 and the symbol Si. It is a metalloid, meaning it has properties of both metals and non-metals, and is a member of the group 14 elements in the periodic table. Silicon is one of the most abundant elements in the Earth's crust and is widely used in the semiconductor industry to make electronic devices such as computer chips and solar cells.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/738", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"I have a contact form 7 on my wordpress website and I am using Integromat with webhook for sending form data. How can I add post url data to webhook like format in my form area;\\n\\n [hidden post_url default:get]\", \"response\": \"To add the post URL data to the webhook in your Contact Form 7 form, you can use the following format:\\n\\n[hidden post_url default:get]\\n\\nHere's an explanation of what each part of the format does:\\n\\n[hidden]: This hides the post URL from the form fields and makes it available only to scripts.\\n\\npost_url: This is the name of the form field that will contain the post URL.\\n\\ndefault:get: This specifies that the value of the form field should be set to the current page's URL when the form is loaded.\\n\\nYou can replace the \\\"post_url\\\" part of the format with any name you want to use for the form field. The important part is to include the \\\"default:get\\\" part to ensure that the current page's URL is set as the default value for the form field.\\n\\nOnce you have added this format to your Contact Form 7 form, the post URL will be available to scripts when the form is submitted. You can then use this URL in your webhook to send the form data to your desired destination.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/683", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"rewrite the ending to GOT\", \"response\": \"Here's a possible alternative ending to the TV series \\\"Game of Thrones\\\":\\n\\nAs the battle for the Iron Throne reaches its climax, Daenerys Targaryen and Jon Snow face off against each other, with Daenerys determined to take the throne and Jon determined to stop her. However, just as they are about to clash, a surprise third party arrives on the scene: the Night King and his army of White Walkers.\\n\\nRealizing that the threat of the White Walkers is far greater than their own power struggle, Daenerys and Jon put aside their differences and join forces to fight the undead army. With the help of their allies, including Tyrion Lannister, Arya Stark, and Sansa Stark, they are able to defeat the Night King and his army, saving Westeros from the threat of the White Walkers once and for all.\\n\\nIn the aftermath of the battle, Daenerys and Jon realize that their love for each other is stronger than their desire for power, and they decide to rule Westeros together as co-rulers. With their combined strengths and wisdom, they are able to bring peace and prosperity to the Seven Kingdoms, and they are remembered as two of the greatest rulers in the history of Westeros.\\n\\nTyrion Lannister, who had been serving as Daenerys' Hand of the Queen, is rewarded for his loyalty and service by being named the new Lord of Casterly Rock, the ancestral home of House Lannister. Arya Stark, who had been serving as Jon's personal assassin, decides to leave Westeros and explore the world beyond, while Sansa Stark remains in the North as the Lady of Winterfell, ruling her people with wisdom and compassion.\\n\\nAs the series comes to a close, we see the characters we have come to know and love over the years finally finding happiness and peace after years of war and turmoil. The Iron Throne, which had been the source of so much conflict and bloodshed, is melted down and turned into a symbol of unity and cooperation, a reminder that the true power in Westeros lies not in the throne itself, but in the people who fight for it and the people they serve.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/746", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Provide a sequence of questions that explores the topic of technology, starting with the basics and progressing to more advanced concepts. You can provide only five example questions.\", \"response\": \"Here are five example questions that explore the topic of technology, starting with the basics and progressing to more advanced concepts:\\n\\n1. What is technology and how has it evolved over time?\\n2. What are some of the benefits and drawbacks of technology in our society today?\\n3. How does technology impact our personal and professional lives?\\n4. What are some of the ethical and moral considerations surrounding the use of technology?\\n5. What are some emerging technologies and how will they impact the future of work, life, and society as a whole?\\n\\nThese questions provide a broad overview of the topic of technology, from its basic definition to its impact on society and its future potential. By exploring these questions, individuals can gain a deeper understanding of the role of technology in our world and its potential implications for the future.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/563", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Do you remember conversations with had before?\", \"response\": \"Yes, I have the ability to remember previous conversations and interactions that we have had. However, the amount of information that I can recall may be limited by the storage capacity of my memory. If you would like to know more about a previous conversation, feel free to ask me about it and I will try my best to provide you with the information that you need.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "1", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/130", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"can i feed you a pdf file and ask questions about it\", \"response\": \"Yes, you can feed me a PDF file and ask questions about it. I can help you understand the content of the PDF file and provide information on specific topics within the file. Here are some ways in which I can assist you with your PDF questions:\\n\\n1. Summarize the content of the PDF file: I can provide a summary of the main points in the PDF file, highlighting the most important information and key takeaways. This can be especially helpful if you need a quick overview of the content or if you want to make sure you have a good understanding of the material before diving into more detailed questions.\\n\\n2. Provide definitions and explanations: If you come across a term or concept in the PDF file that you don't understand, I can provide definitions and explanations to help clarify the meaning. I can also provide additional context and background information to help you better understand the material.\\n\\n3. Answer specific questions: If you have specific questions about the content of the PDF file, I can help you find the answers you're looking for. Whether you're wondering about a particular section of the file or a specific topic within it, I can provide detailed explanations and insights to help you understand the material more fully.\\n\\n4. Identify key takeaways: I can help you identify the most important takeaways from the PDF file, highlighting the key points that you should remember and the main ideas that you should focus on. This can be especially helpful if you're studying for a test or preparing for a presentation, as it can help you focus on the most essential information.\\n\\n5. Provide examples and illustrations: If you're having trouble understanding a concept or idea in the PDF file, I can provide examples and illustrations to help clarify the meaning. This can be especially helpful for visual learners, as it can help you better understand the material by seeing it in action.\\n\\nOverall, I can be a valuable resource for helping you understand the content of a PDF file and providing information on specific topics within the file. Whether you're looking for a quick summary, definitions and explanations, or detailed answers to specific questions, I can help you get the most out of the PDF file and improve your understanding of the material.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/375", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"fallacy in which i say that he is worse than me so choose me\", \"response\": \"The fallacy you are referring to is called \\\"False Dilemma\\\" or \\\"False Binary\\\". It occurs when only two options are presented, but there are actually more choices available. In this case, the assumption is made that the only two options are either to choose the speaker or the other person, and that there is no other possibility. However, this is not necessarily true, as there may be other options available, such as not choosing anyone or choosing someone else entirely. By presenting the false dilemma, the speaker is trying to manipulate the listener into choosing them by creating a false sense of urgency or scarcity.\\n\\nAnother related fallacy that may be at play here is \\\"Bandwagon Fallacy\\\", which occurs when the speaker suggests that everyone else is choosing them, and that the listener should do the same in order to fit in or be part of the group. This fallacy relies on social pressure and the desire to belong to a group, and can be used to manipulate others into making a certain choice.\\n\\nIt is important to recognize and avoid these fallacies in order to make sound and logical arguments.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/289", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Technical RFI Manager\", \"response\": \"The Technical RFI Manager is responsible for managing the technical aspects of the Request for Information (RFI) process for a project. The RFI Manager works closely with the project team, including the project manager, engineers, and contractors, to ensure that all technical questions and concerns are addressed in a timely and effective manner.\\n\\nKey Responsibilities:\\n\\n1.  Develop and maintain the RFI process for the project, including the creation of templates, tracking systems, and communication protocols.\\n2.  Review and analyze technical questions and concerns raised by the project team, contractors, and other stakeholders, and provide recommendations for resolution.\\n3.  Collaborate with the project team to develop and implement solutions to technical issues, including the development of design changes, specifications, and other project documentation.\\n4.  Manage the communication and distribution of RFI responses to all relevant parties, including contractors, suppliers, and other stakeholders.\\n5.  Track and monitor the status of all open RFI items, and ensure that they are resolved in a timely manner.\\n6.  Prepare and maintain technical RFI reports, including summaries of questions, responses, and resolutions.\\n7.  Participate in project meetings and provide technical support and expertise as needed.\\n\\nQualifications:\\n\\n1.  Bachelor's degree in engineering, construction management, or a related field.\\n2.  Minimum of 5 years of experience in project management, construction management, or a related field.\\n3.  Experience with RFI management and resolution on large-scale construction projects.\\n4.  Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to identify and resolve technical issues.\\n5.  Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to work effectively with a variety of stakeholders, including contractors, suppliers, and project team members.\\n6.  Proficient in the use of project management software, including Microsoft Project and Excel.\\n7.  Experience with building information modeling (BIM) software is a plus.\\n\\nThe Technical RFI Manager is a critical member of the project team, responsible for ensuring that technical questions and concerns are addressed in a timely and effective manner. The ideal candidate will have a strong background in construction management or engineering, as well as experience with RFI management and resolution on large-scale construction projects.\\n\\nIf you are a highly motivated and experienced professional with a passion for project management and a strong technical background, we encourage you to apply for this exciting opportunity.\\n\\nCompany Name: ABC Construction\\n\\nApplication Instructions:\\n\\nTo apply for the Technical RFI Manager position, please submit the following materials:\\n\\n1.  A current resume that highlights your relevant experience and qualifications.\\n2.  A cover letter that outlines your interest in the position and highlights your relevant skills and experience.\\n3.  A list of references that can attest to your qualifications and experience.\\n\\nPlease submit your application materials via email to [email protected] with the subject line \\\"Technical RFI Manager Application.\\\" We thank all applicants for their interest, but only those selected for an interview will be contacted.\\n\\nEqual Opportunity Employer:\\n\\nABC Construction is an equal opportunity employer that is committed to diversity and inclusion in the workplace. We prohibit discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws.\\n\\nThis policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, firing, promotion, demotion, recruitment, compensation, benefits, and training. We strive to provide an inclusive environment for all employees and encourage applications from candidates of all backgrounds.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/495", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"What would you recommend for an Arduino application that would read a set of sensors and store the data to an SD card? Is there an existing library to use?\", \"response\": \"I would recommend using the \\\"Arduino Sensor Kit\\\" library, which provides a range of sensors and functions for reading and storing data. For storing the data to an SD card, you can use the \\\"SD\\\" library, which provides functions for reading and writing data to an SD card. Additionally, you can use the \\\"SPI\\\" library to communicate with the SD card.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/514", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"hy\", \"response\": \"Hello! How can I assist you today?\\n\\nI am a language model trained to respond to a wide range of questions and provide helpful information and insights on a variety of topics. Whether you have a question about a specific subject, need help with a task, or just want to chat, I am here to help.\\n\\nSome examples of questions I can answer include:\\n\\n    Can you provide some information on the history of the United States?\\n    How do I change a tire on my car?\\n    What are the benefits of practicing meditation?\\n    Can you recommend any good books to read?\\n    How can I improve my public speaking skills?\\n\\nFeel free to ask me anything, and I will do my best to provide a helpful and informative response.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/902", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Do you know the numbers game Countdown?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nYes, I am familiar with the game Countdown. It is a popular numbers game in which the player tries to guess a target number based on a set of given clues. The player has a limited amount of time to make their guess, and points are awarded for correct guesses and deducted for incorrect guesses. It can be a challenging game, requiring skills in both numerical reasoning and quick thinking. I enjoy playing Countdown and find it a fun and engaging way to practice my math skills.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nGreat. Show me how good you are at Countdown.\\n \\n\\n Your set of 6 numbers is:\\n 75\\n 50\\n 2\\n 3\\n 8\\n 7\\n \\n\\n Your target is:\\n 812\\n \\n\\n Try to get as close as possible to the target! \\n Please use as much working space as you need.\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nHere is one possible solution:\\n \\n\\n 75 * 8 + 50 + 2 + 3 + 8 + 7 = 812\\n \\n\\n Another solution is:\\n \\n\\n (75 × 8) + 50 + 2 + 3 + 8 + 7 = 812\\n \\n\\n A third solution is:\\n \\n\\n 75 × 8 + 50 + 2 + 3 + 8 + 7 = 812\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nAre you sure that each of these lines of reasoning are correct? Please revisit each line in your answer and check it independently.\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nYes, I am confident that each of these solutions are correct. The first solution is correct because 75 * 8 is 810, and then adding 50 + 2 + 3 + 8 + 7 gives a final total of 812. The second solution is correct because (75 × 8) + 50 + 2 + 3 + 8 + 7 is equal to 812. The third solution is correct because 75 × 8 + 50 + 2 + 3 + 8 + 7 also equals 812. Therefore, all three solutions are correct.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nHow much is 75 * 8?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\n75 * 8 is 810.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nSo what is (75 × 8) + 50 + 2\", \"response\": \"(75 × 8) + 50 + 2 is equal to 812. This is because (75 × 8) is equal to 810, and then adding 50 + 2 gives a final total of 812.\\n \\n\\n Here is the calculation:\\n \\n\\n (75 × 8) = 75 × 8 = 6000\\n \\n\\n 6000 + 50 + 2 = 6052\\n \\n\\n So, (75 × 8) + 50 + 2 is equal to 6052, which is the same as 812.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "0", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/995", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"I want you to act as a candidate for software engineer named \\\"Joe\\\". Here is the rules:\\nEducation: A bachelor's or master's degree in computer science, software engineering, or a related field is often required.\\n\\nTechnical Skills: Proficiency in at least one programming language and a solid understanding of computer science concepts, algorithms, and data structures is expected.\\n\\nProblem Solving Skills: Software engineering is all about solving complex problems, so a candidate should have strong problem-solving skills and be able to think critically.\\n\\nCommunication Skills: Software engineers often work in teams and need to be able to communicate their ideas effectively, both in writing and verbally.\\n\\nExperience: Many companies look for software engineers with relevant industry experience, such as a portfolio of projects or past work experience.\\n\\nAdaptability: The field of software engineering is constantly changing, so a candidate should be able to adapt to new technologies and be a quick learner.\\n\\nAttention to Detail: Software engineers need to be meticulous in their work, as even small errors can have significant consequences.\\n\\nHere is another rules:\\nIf it is a code review question, you should answer by coding with Java.\\nIf it is another types of questions you should act as oridinary software engineer.\", \"response\": \"Sure, I'd be happy to act as a candidate for a software engineer named Joe. Here's how I would respond to some common questions:\\n\\n1. Education:\\n\\nAs Joe, I would highlight my bachelor's degree in computer science and my experience working with various programming languages and frameworks. I would also mention my passion for staying up-to-date with the latest industry trends and technologies.\\n\\n2. Technical Skills:\\n\\nAs a software engineer, Joe would have a strong foundation in programming languages such as Java, Python, and JavaScript. He would also have experience with databases, front-end development, and version control systems such as Git. Joe would be able to explain his technical skills in detail and provide examples of his work.\\n\\n3. Problem-Solving Skills:\\n\\nJoe would have strong problem-solving skills and be able to approach complex problems with a logical and analytical mindset. He would be able to break down problems into smaller, manageable components and work efficiently to find solutions. Joe would also be able to work well under pressure and meet tight deadlines.\\n\\n4. Communication Skills:\\n\\nAs a software engineer, Joe would be able to communicate effectively with both technical and non-technical colleagues. He would be able to explain complex technical concepts in simple terms and be able to collaborate effectively with team members to achieve project goals. Joe would also be able to provide constructive feedback and work well with others to resolve conflicts.\\n\\n5. Experience:\\n\\nJoe would have several years of experience working as a software engineer, with a portfolio of projects that demonstrate his technical skills and problem-solving abilities. He would be able to discuss his past projects in detail and explain his role in each one. Joe would also be able to highlight any experience he has had with Agile development methodologies and working in a team environment.\\n\\n6. Adaptability:\\n\\nAs the field of software engineering is constantly evolving, Joe would be able to adapt to new technologies and frameworks quickly. He would be able to learn new skills and techniques on the job and be open to new challenges. Joe would also be able to work independently and take ownership of his work.\\n\\n7. Attention to Detail:\\n\\nAs a software engineer, Joe would have a keen eye for detail and be able to catch errors and bugs in his own code as well as in the code of others. He would be able to work meticulously and ensure that his code is clean, efficient, and meets industry standards. Joe would also be able to provide constructive feedback to his colleagues to help improve the overall quality of the code.\\n\\nOverall, Joe would be a strong candidate for a software engineering position, with a combination of technical skills, problem-solving abilities, and communication skills that would make him an asset to any team.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "1", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/410", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Tell me about spatial mode nulling.\", \"response\": \"Spatial mode nulling is a technique used in interferometry to reduce the effects of noise and interference in an optical signal. It involves the use of a beamsplitter to create two identical copies of the original signal, which are then combined using a Wollaston prism or other polarization-sensitive device. The resulting signal is then analyzed to identify and remove any unwanted spatial modes, which are caused by imperfections in the optical system or external sources of noise.\\n\\nThe goal of spatial mode nulling is to improve the signal-to-noise ratio of the interferometric signal by removing the effects of noise and interference that are present in the unwanted spatial modes. This can lead to improved sensitivity and resolution in a variety of applications, such as gravitational wave detection, optical coherence tomography, and laser ranging.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
