{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/872", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"What is dependency and how does it work in a spring framework?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nSpring uses a dependency injection system to wire together various components of an application, and to make configuration easier and less repetitive. A basic idea of dependency injection is that objects should not need to concern themselves with where their dependencies come from, or how they’re configured. Spring does this using a few different approaches. One is through the use of @value annotations in configuration files, another is through the use of @Autowired, and another is through the use of @Qualifier. This can get a little more complicated when working with interfaces, though.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nWhat is @value used for in Spring?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nThe @value annotation can be used in configuration to define bean properties. Using this, you can define properties that are used by many beans, or that only need to be set once. @Value can also be used to inject a value from a property file, or from a resource file. The value of the annotation can either be a simple string or a reference to another bean. @Value can also be used to inject a reference to a bean defined in another context.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nWhat is the difference between a static reference and non-static reference?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nIn Spring, a static reference refers to a bean that is defined in the application context. A non-static reference refers to a bean that is defined in another context, such as a web application context. Static references can be accessed from any bean in the current context, while non-static references can only be accessed from the bean that they’re injected into.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nWhat is $ and @ used for in Thymeleaf\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nThe $ sign is used to refer to a Thymeleaf context variable. A Thymeleaf context variable is a variable that can be referenced in Thymeleaf templates, and is associated with the current rendering context. These variables are typically defined in the Thymeleaf configuration file, which is called thymeleaf-context.xml. The @ sign is used to refer to an attribute of the current rendering context. In Thymeleaf, a rendering context is the object that controls how a Thymeleaf template is rendered, and is responsible for rendering the template, and resolving Thymeleaf variables.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nwhat is the logger class used for?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nThe logger class in Spring is used for logging. This is a tool for writing information to a log file, so that it can be reviewed later. You can specify different log levels, so that you can write different types of information. For example, you could write debug messages, info messages, warning messages, and error messages.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nhow about the logger class in slf4j?\", \"response\": \"SLF4J is a logging framework that provides a simple and consistent interface for logging. It is a wrapper around other logging frameworks, such as Log4j, Logback, and JDK logging. The logger class in SLF4J is used for logging. It provides a simple and consistent interface for logging, and can be used with any of the supported logging frameworks. SLF4J is a good choice for logging, because it provides a simple and consistent interface, and it is easy to switch between different logging frameworks.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/404", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"What skills should a person that specializes in AI prompting and machin learning learn? What certifications would you recommend?\", \"response\": \"Here are some skills and certifications that may be useful for someone specializing in AI prompting and machine learning:\\n\\n1. Programming languages: Python, R, and Java are commonly used for AI and machine learning.\\n\\n2. Machine learning algorithms: Familiarity with various machine learning algorithms such as decision trees, random forests, neural networks, and support vector machines.\\n\\n3. Data preprocessing: Understanding of data preprocessing techniques such as data cleaning, feature engineering, and data transformation.\\n\\n4. Deep learning: Knowledge of deep learning techniques such as convolutional neural networks, recurrent neural networks, and long short-term memory networks.\\n\\n5. Natural language processing (NLP): Understanding of NLP techniques such as tokenization, sentence segmentation, part-of-speech tagging, named entity recognition, and sentiment analysis.\\n\\n6. AI frameworks: Familiarity with AI frameworks such as TensorFlow, PyTorch, and Caffe.\\n\\n7. Cloud computing: Knowledge of cloud computing platforms such as AWS, Azure, and Google Cloud Platform for deploying and scaling AI models.\\n\\n8. Certification: There are several certifications available for AI and machine learning, such as the Certified Machine Learning Specialist (CMLS) from the Machine Learning Academy, the Certified Artificial Intelligence Professional (CAIP) from the American Institute of Artificial Intelligence, and the Certified Data Scientist (CDS) from the Data Science Council.\\n\\n9. Project management: Understanding of project management principles and practices, including agile methodologies, for managing AI and machine learning projects.\\n\\n10. Communication: Strong communication skills for presenting and explaining AI and machine learning concepts to technical and non-technical audiences.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/33", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"I live in Australia. I am thinking about purchasing a car. It will be mostly a town car, but it might every once in a great while have to make a trip from Canberra to Sydney. I would like to be environmentally friendly and go electric, but I am concerned about the lack of charging stations for electric cars. A hybrid car may be the solution since I don't have to use a charging station. I am not necessarily committed to buying a new car and would consider buying a pre-owned car. Our driveway makes a car with a low clearance problematic, so an SUV might be a possibility. What would you recommend?\", \"response\": \"If you're concerned about the lack of charging stations for electric cars in Australia and you occasionally need to travel from Canberra to Sydney, a hybrid car might be a good option for you. Hybrid cars combine an internal combustion engine with an electric motor and a battery, so they can run on either fuel or electricity, depending on the driving conditions.\\n\\nWhen it comes to purchasing a hybrid car, you have several options. You can opt for a new car or consider a pre-owned car, which can be a more affordable option. There are several popular hybrid car models available in Australia, including the Toyota Prius, the Honda Insight, and the Ford Fusion.\\n\\nIf you're worried about the low clearance of an SUV, you might want to consider a hybrid SUV instead. Some popular hybrid SUVs in Australia include the Toyota RAV4 Hybrid, the Honda CR-V Hybrid, and the Hyundai Tucson Hybrid.\\n\\nWhen choosing a hybrid car, it's important to consider factors such as fuel efficiency, driving range, and the size of the battery. You should also make sure that the car is compatible with the charging infrastructure in your area, in case you need to charge it.\\n\\nIn summary, a hybrid car might be a good option for you if you're looking for an environmentally friendly car that can still make the occasional long-distance trip. Consider factors such as fuel efficiency, driving range, and the size of the battery when choosing a hybrid car, and opt for a hybrid SUV if you need more cargo space or a higher driving position.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}